        }
      },
      "rule": "An arcaded loggia of three to five equal semicircular arches, on the ground or upper floor, oriented for shade and view -- the family's principal columnar element and its designed outdoor room.",
      "note": "Distinguished explicitly from tuscan-vernacular's working portico: 'the villa has a loggia designed for sitting in; the farm has a portico for working under' (distinguished_from)."
